`DiagonalGaussianDistribution.__init__` computes `std = exp(0.5*logvar)` and
`var = exp(logvar)` eagerly.  Measured on the Wan VAE encode path
(out/videogen_more_enc, region `dgd_init`, 2.7% irregular):

    dgd_init = 14.2*numel + 114,569      of which 13.6 of the 14.2 is
                                         mkl_vml_kernel_sExp

`AutoencoderKLWan.forward` and the Wan pipelines read `posterior.mode()`, which
touches neither; `sample()` touches `std` only.  So at least one of the two
full-size `exp` passes over the encoder output is always discarded, and for the
`mode()` callers both are.

Computing them on first read keeps every value, and keeps `var is std` in the
deterministic case.  equiv_more.py hashes mode / sample / std / var / logvar /
kl at five (frames, resolution) points and three tiled configurations: all
identical.

--- a/src/diffusers/models/autoencoders/vae.py
+++ b/src/diffusers/models/autoencoders/vae.py
@@ -689,12 +689,44 @@
         self.parameters = parameters
         self.mean, self.logvar = torch.chunk(parameters, 2, dim=1)
         self.logvar = torch.clamp(self.logvar, -30.0, 20.0)
         self.deterministic = deterministic
-        self.std = torch.exp(0.5 * self.logvar)
-        self.var = torch.exp(self.logvar)
-        if self.deterministic:
-            self.var = self.std = torch.zeros_like(
-                self.mean, device=self.parameters.device, dtype=self.parameters.dtype
-            )
+        # `std` and `var` are two full-size `exp` passes over the latent.
+        # `mode()` reads neither and `sample()` reads only `std`, so at least one
+        # of them is discarded at every call site in the Wan pipelines.  Compute
+        # on first read; the values, and the object identity `var is std` in the
+        # deterministic case, are what the eager version produced.
+        self._std = None
+        self._var = None
+
+    def _compute_std_var(self):
+        if self.deterministic:
+            self._var = self._std = torch.zeros_like(
+                self.mean, device=self.parameters.device, dtype=self.parameters.dtype
+            )
+        else:
+            self._std = torch.exp(0.5 * self.logvar)
+            self._var = torch.exp(self.logvar)
+
+    @property
+    def std(self) -> torch.Tensor:
+        if self._std is None:
+            self._compute_std_var()
+        return self._std
+
+    @std.setter
+    def std(self, value: torch.Tensor) -> None:
+        self._std = value
+
+    @property
+    def var(self) -> torch.Tensor:
+        if self._var is None:
+            self._compute_std_var()
+        return self._var
+
+    @var.setter
+    def var(self, value: torch.Tensor) -> None:
+        self._var = value
